  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anil Kumar Srivastava vs The State Of Bihar on 6 February, 2013 Author: Dinesh Kumar Singh Bench: Dinesh Kumar Singh Patna High Court Cr.Misc. No.46630 of 2012 (3) dt.06-02-2013 In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.46630 of 2012 ====================================================== Anil Kumar Srivastava .... .... Petitio Versus The State Of Bihar .... .... Opposite Par ====================================================== Coram: Honourable Mr. Justice Dinesh Kumar Singh Oral Order",
    "facts": "The petitioner is apprehending his arrest in a case registered for the offences punishable under Sections 406, 420, 409, 272 of the Indian Penal Code and 51/59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act. Petitioner was posted as Assistant Godown Manager of S.F.C., Chautham when the S.D.O. took the sample of the wheat from the godown, which was not found confirming to the prescribed standard of the quality.",
    "arguments": "It is submitted by learned counsel for the petitioner that the petitioner is not responsible for maintaining the standard of the grains as the grains were supplied by the F.C.I. and this is not in dispute that the seized grains were not supplied by the F.C.I.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is submitted by learned counsel for the petitioner that the petitioner is not responsible for maintaining the standard of the grains as the grains were supplied by the F.C.I. and this is not in dispute that the seized grains were not supplied by the F.C.I.",
